# the registry of formats
#
# every format mink knows is one registration, listed on one line in the
# registry's generator, the only list of formats. the generator checks every
# registration and writes the tables the registry is, in format/builtin: the
# registrations, the readers index the link phases sniff inputs through and
# the relocation lookups of every pair. it refuses a registration whose pairs
# do not hold, so nothing is built or checked when mink runs.
#
# the registry sits below the link phases, and every input is read and
# every model converted through it, with one argument order: the registry,
# then the allocator a result lives in, then what is read or converted. it
# answers what takes the registrations: the format of an input, a file read,
# converted, loaded or saved whole, relocation lookups and trait encodings,
# so no dependent names a format's own modules.

